---
// THE THREE WEBFONT PRELOADS, IN ONE PLACE, MOUNTED ON EVERY PAGE.
//
// `font-display: optional` (styles/fonts.css) made these load-bearing, and that
// is a change of KIND, not of degree. Under `swap` a preload was an
// optimization: without one a page painted in the fallback and swapped a few
// hundred ms later, so every first visit still ENDED on the real face and the
// preload only moved *when*. Under `optional` the browser gives the font ~100ms
// and, if it has not arrived, keeps the fallback for the whole document and
// never swaps — so a page that does not preload never reaches its own typeface
// on a first visit at all.
//
// That is measured, not theoretical. `optional` was first written with the
// preloads on `/studio/` alone, and on an UNTHROTTLED localhost against the
// built dist the landing page and the docs body then rendered the fallback
// while `/studio/` rendered Outfit and Playfair: the whole site quietly
// downgraded on every first visit, the one route with a preload excepted. An
// independent checker caught it; no gate in the tree could.
//
// SO `optional` AND THE PRELOAD ARE ONE DECISION. A change that moves these
// links back to a single route has to move `font-display` back to `swap` in the
// same commit, or it re-introduces that regression on every other page.
//
// TWO MOUNT POINTS, ONE DEFINITION — because the site has two <head> surfaces
// and neither covers the other: `site/ResourceHints.astro` for the standalone
// routes (landing, studio, components) and `ThemeProvider.astro` for the
// Starlight docs zone, which is a `components:` override in astro.config.mjs
// and never renders ResourceHints. That split is pre-existing (PwaHead is
// mounted the same way for the same reason); this file exists so the preloads
// are not forked across it (HARD RULE #15).
//
// FILES, NOT FACES — which is why three links cover twelve `@font-face` blocks.
// Each family's vendored weights are the SAME variable file stored under
// per-weight names (every Outfit weight is md5 `fdf9c509…`, upright Playfair
// 400/700 is `ef05b30d…`, mono 400/500/600 is one 31432-byte file), and
// `fonts.css`'s blocks each pin a different position on that one file's weight
// axis. Vite content-hashes and dedupes, so importing 600/700/400 here resolves
// to the three assets the whole site is served from — which is why the built
// href reads `outfit-300` and `playfair-display-400`, the dedup winner's name.
//
// Vite hands back the SAME hashed, base-aware URL that `styles/fonts.css`
// resolves its own relative `url()` to. That identity is the whole point: a
// preload whose href does not match the URL the stylesheet requests is not a
// no-op, it is a second download plus a "preloaded but not used" warning.
// `font-preload.spec.ts` asserts the match, because nothing else would notice.
import outfitUrl from '../../playground/fonts/outfit-600.woff2?url';
import playfairUrl from '../../playground/fonts/playfair-display-700.woff2?url';
import monoUrl from '../../playground/fonts/jetbrains-mono-400.woff2?url';
---

<link rel="preload" href={outfitUrl} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link rel="preload" href={playfairUrl} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link rel="preload" href={monoUrl} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
